{"id": "EUVD-2026-103854", "enisaUuid": "dfc2374b-2ce6-34ab-b058-c998d8bbeecd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_uac1_legacy: validate bRequest index in generic_{set,get}_cmd\n\ngeneric_set_cmd() and generic_get_cmd() use the low nibble of\nctrl->bRequest as an index into con->data[]:\n\n    u8 cmd = (ctrl->bRequest & 0x0F);  /* 0 .. 15 */\n    ...\n    con->data[cmd] = value;            /* OOB when cmd >= 5 */\n\nstruct usb_audio_control (include/linux/usb/audio.h) declares data as\na 5-element array, so indices 5 through 15 write (or read) up to 44\nbytes past the end of the array on the heap.\n\nA malicious USB host can craft a class-specific SET_CUR / GET_CUR\nrequest with an arbitrary bRequest value, triggering the out-of-bounds\naccess from an IRQ completion handler with no further preconditions.\n\nAdd an ARRAY_SIZE() guard to both functions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da841c1511a6160b8bc6bb7b7c6d4c9fb76fb51e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36f3f009049bc91e14dc856007932473318d12f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c611876c002d712ae5f246af5188432c708f79d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/697cfe6e53b66cda196d6f8833b0ee97fefd0a8a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9062d50e75c24dc7911be05c9b1719b3b256af15"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m6wv-vgq8-7pqj", "CVE-2026-98769"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0600300f-357f-38b5-a9c9-71aafcc06dab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1f8a6c69-c52a-3800-999e-1b2e6fd20f23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c47d7b09891abb4f8b222317c89c7469bed8db3a <9062d50e75c24dc7911be05c9b1719b3b256af15"}, {"id": "4066a723-b4b8-3e80-8a35-d4a764048ef8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "4e8de34a-5e06-386a-9257-c343c9a0721c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5ca2cb4e-1986-30eb-9fcd-876fa18d3b7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c47d7b09891abb4f8b222317c89c7469bed8db3a <36f3f009049bc91e14dc856007932473318d12f8"}, {"id": "5d5d7892-12d6-3da7-9daf-9bd07f76fedb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "7048c9d3-52df-349e-a639-fe8c66bd1a56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c47d7b09891abb4f8b222317c89c7469bed8db3a <697cfe6e53b66cda196d6f8833b0ee97fefd0a8a"}, {"id": "9d070865-6f53-328e-b819-5d2eab7563db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.31"}, {"id": "9ea362cb-1e36-37a5-8c41-6b033d680214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c47d7b09891abb4f8b222317c89c7469bed8db3a <8c611876c002d712ae5f246af5188432c708f79d"}, {"id": "aa1d5ab8-e709-37fa-a440-62f38e4bdc75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c47d7b09891abb4f8b222317c89c7469bed8db3a <da841c1511a6160b8bc6bb7b7c6d4c9fb76fb51e"}, {"id": "b076ab13-dbf0-371a-bb9c-524ad71dac2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "ba51bd03-e3ce-3102-9089-452f31e5636c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9060bef6-806f-3bb0-97b2-15a17c1b8861", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}